d</Street><City>Lewes</City><Sub>Delaware</Sub><Country>USA</Country></Address><Name><First>Malique</First><Last>Bowen</Last><Middle>R</Middle></Name></Contact></Organization><STUDY center_name="BioProject" alias="PRJNA1479055" accession="SRP710139"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRP710139</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioProject" label="primary">PRJNA1479055</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS><DESCRIPTOR><STUDY_TITLE>Redox Influence on Microbial Communities in Anaerobic Coastal Sediments</STUDY_TITLE><STUDY_TYPE existing_study_type="Other"/><STUDY_ABSTRACT>We inoculated anaerobic sediments from 3 different depths using two different reducing agents (sodium dithionite and titanium (III) citrate) at varied redoxes (-150, -300, -340, -380, and -570mV) over 150 days to assess longterm affects on microbial community composition.</STUDY_ABSTRACT></DESCRIPTOR></STUDY><SAMPLE alias="DB5SauceyJanB06_S148_L001_R1_001.fastq.gz" accession="SRS29574928"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRS29574928</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioSample">SAMN60939726</EXTERNAL_ID><SUBMITTER_ID namespace="pda|malbow" label="Sample name">DB5SauceyJanB06_S148_L001_R1_001.fastq.gz</SUBMITTER_ID></IDENTIFIERS><TITLE>DB5 30 Days</TITLE><SAMPLE_NAME><TAXON_ID>749907</TAXON_ID><SCIENTIFIC_NAME>sediment metagenome</SCIENTIFIC_NAME></SAMPLE_NAME><SAMPLE_LINKS><SAMPLE_LINK><XREF_LINK><DB>bioproject</DB><ID>1479055</ID><LABEL>PRJNA1479055</LABEL></XREF_LINK></SAMPLE_LINK></SAMPLE_LINKS><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTES><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>isolation_source</TAG><VALUE>Coastal Marine Sediment</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>collection_date</TAG><VALUE>2023-11-11</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>geo_loc_name</TAG><VALUE>USA: Broadkill River, Delaware</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>lat_lon</TAG><VALUE>38.80216 N 75.20326 W</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>rel_to_oxygen</TAG><VALUE>anaerobe</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>Isolate</TAG><VALUE>DB5</VAL